  "header_row_count": 1,
  "column_count": 7,
  "shared_notes": [
    "Note. Panel A shows regression coefficients per 1-point increase in exposure score from linear mixed-effects models with participant-level random intercepts, fitted as unadjusted, age- and sex-adjusted, and multivariable-adjusted models. Panel B summarises quantile g-computation-style coefficients and signed weights, calculated by dividing each exposure coefficient by the sum of the absolute values of all exposure coefficients. Higher EVI scores indicate greater greenness, whereas higher O₃ scores indicate lower ozone exposure. Quantile g-computation was fitted without bootstrap resampling. Confidence intervals derive from the underlying linear mixed models; signed weights are a descriptive decomposition of relative coefficient magnitudes, not causal contribution shares."
  ],
